G3918.def:
πάρ-ειμι 
[in LXX for בּוֹא, etc. ;] 
__1. to be by, at hand or present; 
__(a) of persons: Apocalypse 17:8; παρών (opposite to ἀπών), 1 Corinthiens 5:3, 2 Corinthiens 10:2 10:11 13:2 13:10; before ἐπί with genitive, Actes 24:19; ἐνώπιον, Actes 10:33; ἐνθάδε, Actes 17:6; πρός, with accusative of person(s), Actes 12:20, 2 Corinthiens 11:8, Galates 4:18, 20; 
__(b) of things : of time, ὁ καιρός, Jean 7:6; τ. παρόν, Hébreux 12:11; ἡ ἀλήθεια, 2 Pierre 1:12; ταῦτα, 2 Pierre 1:9; τ. παρόντα, Hébreux 13:5. 
__2. to have come or arrived (Hdt., Thuc., al.; see Field, Notes, 65) : Luc 13:1, Jean 11:28, Actes 10:21; before εἰς, Colossiens 1:6; before ἐπί, with accusative of thing(s), Matthieu 26:50 (cf. συν-πάρειμι).†

G3925.def:
παρ-εμ-βολή, -ῆς, ἡ
(παρεμβάλλω), [in LXX chiefly for מַחֲנֶה ;] 
__1. an insertion, interpolation (Æschin.) 
__2. In the Macedonian dialect (Rutherford, NPhr., 473), as a military term; 
__(a) an army in battle array: Hébreux 11:34 (cf. Exode 14:19-20, Juges 4:16, al.; frequently in Polyb.); 
__(b) a camp (Exode 29:14, al.) : Hébreux 13:11, 13 Apocalypse 20:9; 
__(with) barracks, soldiers' quarters: Actes 21:34, 37 22:24 23:10, 16 23:32 28:16 (WH, txt., R, om.).†
παρ-εμ-βάλλω, 
[in LXX frequently and chiefly for מַחֲנֶה ;] 
__1. to put in beside or between, interpose. 
__2. In late writers (Polyb., al., LXX) as technical military term; 
__(a) of soldiers, to draw up in line (frequently in 1Ma.2:32, al.); 
__(b) of siege works, to cast up: with accusative and dative, χάρακά σοι, Luc 19:43.†

G3928.def:
παρ-ἐρχομαι 
[in LXX chiefly for עָבַר ;] 
__1. to pass, pass by; 
__(a) of persons: absol., Luc 18:37; with accusative of person(s), Marc 6:48; with accusative lot., Actes 16:8; before διά, with genitive, Matthieu 8:28; 
__(b) of things : τ. ποτήριον, Matthieu 26:39 (ἀπ᾽ ἐμοῦ), Matthieu 26:42; of time, Matthieu 14:15, Marc 14:35, Actes 27:9, 1 Pierre 4:3. Metaphorical, 
__(a) to pass away, perish: Matthieu 5:18 24:34-35 Marc 13:30-31, Luc 16:17 21:32-33, 2 Corinthiens 5:17, Jacques 1:10, 2 Pierre 3:10; 
__(b) to pass by, neglect, disregard: with accusative of thing(s), Luc 11:42 15:29. 
__2. to come to, arrive: Luc 12:37 17:7, Actes 24:7, R, mg. (cf. ἀντι-παρέρχομαι).†
SYN.: παραβαίνω

G3958.def:
πάσχω 
[in LXX: Amos 6:6 (חָלָה ni.), Wis.12:27, Sir.38:16, al. ;] 
to suffer, be acted on, as opposite to acting, often limited by a word expressive of good or evil; 
__(a) of misfortunes (most frequently without any limiting word) : absol., Luc 22:15 24:46, Actes 1:3 3:18 17:3, 1 Corinthiens 12:26, Hébreux 2:18 9:26 13:12, 1 Pierre 2:19-20 2:23 3:17 4:15 4:19; before ὑπό, with genitive, Matthieu 17:12; ὑπέρ, Actes 9:16, Philippiens 1:20, 2 Thessaloniciens 1:5, 1 Pierre 2:21; with dative ref., 1 Pierre 4:1; περί, with genitive (before ὑπέρ), 1 Pierre 3:18; διά, with accusative, 1 Pierre 3:14; ὀλίγον (a little while), 1 Pierre 5:10; with accusative, Matthieu 27:19, Marc 9:12, Luc 13:2 24:26, Actes 28:5, 2 Timothée 1:12, Hébreux 5:8, Apocalypse 2:10; παθήματα, 2 Corinthiens 1:6; ταῦτα, Galates 3:4 (EV; cf. Lft., in l, but see infr.); accusative before ἀπό, Matthieu 16:21, Luc 9:22 17:25; ὑπό, Marc 5:26, 1 Thessaloniciens 2:14; 
__(b) of pleasant experiences (but always with qualifying word, εὖ or accusative of thing(s)) : Galates 3:4 (cf. Grimm-Thayer, see word; Interp. Corn., in l, but see supr.) (cf. προ-, συν-πάσχω).†

G3962.def:
πατήρ, πατρός, -τρί, τέρα, [in LXX chiefly and very frequently for אָב ;] 
a father; 
__1. prop., 
__(a) of the male parent: Matthieu 2:22, Luc 1:17, Jean 4:53; anarth., Hébreux 12:7 (M, Pr., 82 f.); pl., of both parents (cl.), Hébreux 11:23; οἱ π. τ. σαρκός, Hébreux 12:9; 
__(b) of a forefather or ancestor (in cl. usually in pl.; Hom., al.): Matthieu 3:9, Luc 1:73, Jean 8:39, al.; pl., Matthieu 23:30, 32 Luc 6:23, 26 Jean 4:20, 1 Corinthiens 10:1, al.
__2. Metaphorical, 
__(a) of an author, originator, or archetype (= αἴτιος, ἀρχηγός, etc.; Pind., Plat., al.): Jean 8:41-44, Romains 4:11, 12 16. 
__(b) as a title of respect or honour, used of seniors, teachers and others in a position of responsible authority (Juges 17:10, 2 Rois 2:12, Proverbes 1:8, al.): Matthieu 23:9 Actes 7:2 22:1, 1 Jean 2:13. 
__3. Of God (as in cl. of Zeus) as Father; 
__(a) of created things: τ. φώτων, Jacques 1:17; 
__(b) of all sentient beings: Éphésiens 3:14, 15 Hébreux 12:9; 
__(with) of men, esp. those in covenant relation with Him (freq in OT and later Jewish lit.; see Dalman, Words, 184ff.): Matthieu 6:4, Luc 6:36, Jean 4:21, Jacques 3:9, al.; ὁ π. ὁ ἐν (τ.) οὐρανοῖς, Matthieu 5:16, Marc 11:25; ὁ π. ὁ οὐράνιος, Matthieu 6:14 15:13; esp. in the Epp., of Christians: Romains 8:15, 2 Corinthiens 6:18, Galates 4:6, Éphésiens 2:18 4:6, 1 Jean 2:1; with genitive qual., τ. οἰκτιρμῶν, 2 Corinthiens 1:3; τ. δοξῆς, Éphésiens 1:17; 
__(d) of Christ (Dalman, Words, 190 ff.); 
__(α) by our Lord himself: ὁ π., Matthieu 11:25-27, Luc 10:2, 22 Jean 5:20-23, al.; ὁ π. μου, Matthieu 11:27, al.; ὁ ἐν τ. οὐρανοῖς, Matthieu 7:11, al.; ὁ οὐράνιος, Matthieu 15:13; vocat., Jean 11:41 12:27, 28 17:1, 5, 11, 20, 25 (cf. Abbott, JG., 96 f.); 
__(β) by Apostles: Jean 1:14 (anarth.; see M, Pr., l.with), Romains 15:6, 2 Corinthiens 1:3 11:31, Éphésiens 1:3, Colossiens 1:3, Hébreux 1:5, 1 Pierre 1:3, Apocalypse 1:6 (cf. Westc., Epp. Jo., 27-34).

G3985G.def:
πειράζω poët. and late prose form of πειράω, which see, 
[in LXX for נָסָה pi. ;] 
__1. to make proof of (Hom.). 
__2. to try, attempt (Luc., Polyb., with inf. (see M, Pr., 205; B1., § 69, 4), Actes 9:26 16:7 24:6. 
__3. In LXX and NT, like Heb. נָסָה, with accusative of person(s), to test, try, prove; 
__(a) in a good sense : Jean 6:6, 2 Corinthiens 13:5, Hébreux 11:17, Apocalypse 2:2; esp. of trials and af6ictions sent or permitted by God (Genèse 22:1, Exode 20:20, Wis.3:5, al.), 1 Corinthiens 10:13, Hébreux 2:18 4:15 11:17, 37, Apocalypse 3:10; 
__(b) in a bad sense (Apoll. Rhod., 3, 10): of the attempts made to ensnare Jesus in his speech, Matthieu 16:1 19:3 22:18, 35 Marc 8:11 10:2 12:15, Luc 11:16, Jean 8:6; of temptation to sin, to tempt, Jacques 1:13-14 (see Hort, in l), Galates 6:1, Apocalypse 2:10; esp. of temptations of the devil, Matthieu 4:1, 3 Marc 1:13, Luc 4:2, 1 Corinthiens 7:5, 1 Thessaloniciens 3:5; ὁ πειράζων, the tempter, Matthieu 4:3, 1 Thessaloniciens 3:5; 
__(with) in bad sense also (Exode 17:2, 7, Nombres 14:22, al.), of distrustful testing, trying or challenging of God: Actes 15:10, 1 Corinthiens 10:9 (WH, mg., ἐξεπείρασαν), Hébreux 3:9; τ. πνεῦμα Κυρίου, Actes 5:9 (of. ἐκ-πειράζω).†
SYN.: δοκιμάζω, q.v

