G3992.def:
πέμπω 
[in LXX chiefly for שָׁלַח ;] 
to send; 
__(a) of persons: with accusative, absol., Matthieu 22:7, Luc 7:19, Jean 1:22, 2 Corinthiens 9:3, al.; ptcp. before verb., Matthieu 14:10, Actes 19:31, al.; ptcp. before διά (= Heb. יָד;, 1 Rois 16:20, al.), Matthieu 11:2 (cf. Apocalypse 1:1); of teachers sent by God, Jean 1:33 4:34, Romains 8:3, al.; with accusative and dative, 1 Corinthiens 4:17, Philippiens 2:19; before πρός, with accusative, Luc 4:26, Jean 16:7, al.; before λέγων (cf. Heb. אָמַר שָׁלַח Genèse 38:25, al.), Luc 7:6, 19; before εἰς, with accusative loc., Matthieu 2:8, Luc 15:15, al.; before εἰς (of purpose), Éphésiens 6:22, Colossiens 4:8, 1 Pierre 2:14; with inf., Jean 1:33, 1 Corinthiens 16:3, Apocalypse 22:16; 
__(b) of things : Apocalypse 11:10; before εἰς, Apocalypse 1:11; id., of purpose, Actes 11:29, Philippiens 4:16; with dative of person(s), 2 Thessaloniciens 2:11; π. τ. δρέπανον σου (cf. εξαποστείλατε δρέπανα = מַגָּל שָׁלַח, Joël 3:13), Apocalypse 14:15, 18 (cf. ἀνα-, ἐκ-, μετα-, προ-, συν-πέμπω) 
SYN.: ἀποστέλλω, q.v

G3996.def:
πενθέω, -ῶ 
[in LXX chiefly for אָבַל ;] 
to mourn (for), lament; 
__(a) intrans. : Matthieu 5:4 (5) Matthieu 9:15, 1 Corinthiens 5:2; π. καὶ κλαίειν, Matthieu 16:10, Luc 6:25, Jacques 4:9, Apocalypse 18:15, 19; before ἐπί, with accusative, Apocalypse 18:11; 
__(b) trans., with accusative, 2 Corinthiens 12:21.†
SYN.: see: θρηνέω
